# Same range cuts as the DC3/DC4 sources (optimizes sim time):
DefaultRangeCut 0.005
Region Spacecraft
Spacecraft.Volume SCbody
Spacecraft.RangeCut 1.

Region Pipebody
Pipebody.Volume PIPbody
Pipebody.RangeCut 1.

DetectorTimeConstant 0.000002

# Particle event LOCLPAR0001, 600 s, in 5 pieces (one component each) built at the attitude of their
# time span (yaw change <= 10 deg per piece); together they make up the event.

# Piece 1 of 5: 0-418.911 s after the event start.
# Local particle event: quasi-trapped electrons, exp(-E/50 keV),
# peak I(>30 keV) = 3.9e+03 e/cm2/s/sr at 90 deg pitch, sin^4 pitch-angle distribution.
# Rocking -21.88 deg, yaw -71.34 deg, field dip 0 deg. Directions in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source LOCLPAR0001_p1
LOCLPAR0001_p1.ParticleType 3
LOCLPAR0001_p1.Beam FarFieldNormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction LOCLPAR0001_p1_beam.dat
LOCLPAR0001_p1.Spectrum NormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction
# Light-curve times are relative to t_ref = 1835948205.0 (unix s, first orientation row of this burst).
# Simulate with DC3_final_530km_3_month_with_slew_15sbins_GalacticEarth_cut_normed.ori and add t_ref to the simulated times afterwards.
# Original light curves (absolute unix times): LOCLPAR0001_p1_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0001_p2_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0001_p3_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0001_p4_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0001_p5_lightcurve.dat; see sim_time_reference.txt.
LOCLPAR0001_p1.Lightcurve File false LOCLPAR0001_p1_lightcurve_shifted.dat

# Piece 2 of 5: 418.911-501.099 s after the event start.
# Local particle event: quasi-trapped electrons, exp(-E/50 keV),
# peak I(>30 keV) = 3.9e+03 e/cm2/s/sr at 90 deg pitch, sin^4 pitch-angle distribution.
# Rocking -21.88 deg, yaw -61.05 deg, field dip 0 deg. Directions in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source LOCLPAR0001_p2
LOCLPAR0001_p2.ParticleType 3
LOCLPAR0001_p2.Beam FarFieldNormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction LOCLPAR0001_p2_beam.dat
LOCLPAR0001_p2.Spectrum NormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction
LOCLPAR0001_p2.Lightcurve File false LOCLPAR0001_p2_lightcurve_shifted.dat

# Piece 3 of 5: 501.099-546.282 s after the event start.
